A||||8||86GT-FstBk||Smokin' 2.8||||5||
Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||07-16-2000||10:24 AM||||this is a simple question.  My 2.8 cranks just fine when it is cold and is around 40-50 on the pressure but when it gets to operating temp the pressure drops to about 20 at idle.  When I crank it when its warm and has sat for about 10 minutes it kicks out a nice large puff of smoke. What's up with it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||07-16-2000||11:43 AM||||Leaking injectors or worn valve guide seals.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86GT-FstBk||07-16-2000||07:03 PM||||i just checked the compression of each cylinder.  All cylinders registered 130psi.  What could be causing my low oil pressure and smoking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-16-2000||07:14 PM||||I wouldn't worry too much about the oil pressure. Doesn't sound too uncommon.<BR>As for the smoke... what color is it? does it smell like gas or oil? <BR>Could just be starting up rich.||||reg||1
Z||000004||86GT-FstBk||07-16-2000||07:37 PM||||well Raydar,  The smoke has a fuel smell to it. The smoke comes out  mainly when starting and when I rev the engine.  I know my compression is good.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||07-16-2000||10:00 PM||||86GT... Already sent e-mail.<BR>There is a temp sensor that, among other things, controls the cold start injector. If that is going bad, it could be telling the ECM that the engine temp is colder than it really is. The ECM would compensate by enriching the mixture, and dumping in more gas. This is not the same sensor that runs the temp gauge, if I remember correctly. <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||07-16-2000||10:30 PM||||Huh?  Not to select sweaters (pick knits), here, but for the sake of accuracy, the ECM does <B>not</B> control the cold start injector.  Only the cold start switch does.<P>But you are correct that the ECM needs to know the engine temperature, and it gets that data from another sensor.  And there is indeed a 3rd sensor that runs the temperature gage, as you stated    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-16-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||07-17-2000||07:41 AM||||whew, and here I thought I was going crazy when I removed 3 temperature sensors from the 2.8...||||reg||10
Z||000008||Raydar||07-17-2000||09:51 AM||||Stu... Thanks for keeping me straight. My statement was made from my recollection of a friend who was resurrecting a dead 85 GT. Said he fixed a temp sensor that was causing the cold start injector to go nuts. I just took that, and *ran* with it. <BR>I would still look for something related to temp sensors. <BR> <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
